      "message": "If I understand it correctly, `CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE` is the base address for code in RAM (256 kB), and `CONFIG_MAPPED_STORAGE_BASE` is the base address for all flash memory. Is this correct? Does this mean that we were previously verifying the signature from RAM (address `0x10080000 + 0`) on NPCX targets and are now verifying from flash (address `0x64000000 + 0x40000`)?\n\nHave you verified that this doesn\u0027t break other NPCX targets?",
